marinades are an easy way to add flavor  to any chicken dinner today we're gonna  show you the basics of how to marinate  chicken there are four core elements to  any good marinade fat acid sugar and  seasoning the first element to a great  marinade is fat we're gonna use olive  oil but there's so many different  options that you can use fat is  important because it helps the meat  retain moisture while cooking and it  holds onto any seasoning that you're  gonna add to the marinade the next  element we're gonna need is acid you  could use lime juice vinegar we're gonna  use the lemon juice for this marinade  acid is essential because it helps cut  through the fat it also helps brighten  the dish up now we're gonna add  something sweet you could use brown  sugar maple syrup agave granulated sugar  for this recipe we're gonna use honey  sugar is really important because it  helps caramelization as you're cooking  that's what's gonna get that meat that  really beautiful brown color so the last  thing we need to do is add seasoning  this is maybe the most important part of  the marinade this is where you can get  really creative and make this dish your  own seasoning helps build the layers of  flavor we're gonna do a pretty simple  seasoning for this one with salt pepper  and minced garlic but again you can  really use your imagination here we just  made a simple garlic lemon pepper  marinade but once you have those four  options you can make so many different  kinds like a coconut curry honey mustard  soy glaze and fajita now that your  marinade is ready it's time to add the  chicken you can use any cut we're gonna  use chicken breasts it's really  important to make sure that you're fully  coating every single part of the chicken  once you coat it cover it and put it in  the fridge for 30 minutes - up to four  hours after four hours it's really not  gonna get any more flavor so save  yourself some time when you finally go  to cook your chicken whether it's on the  grill the oven stovetop it's gonna  really have such an incredible flavor  and it's gonna have that beautiful brown  color so now that you know the four core  elements fat acids sweetness and  seasoning you can really get creative  and make some incredibly delicious easy  weeknight dinners  [Music]
 

